            {
                "entry_id": "a623aed1-db71-3760-8b8d-86cf47dbeedd",
                "word": "Romanist",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "a4c31f81-7613-4300-a05d-442e230daf25",
                        "entry_id": "a623aed1-db71-3760-8b8d-86cf47dbeedd",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "Romanists"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "86ba2547-8854-304a-9861-4495be012f8e",
                        "entry_id": "a623aed1-db71-3760-8b8d-86cf47dbeedd",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A Roman Catholic."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "derogatory",
                            "often"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a94ac52b-4f61-4050-bdf3-c5101d002e2c",
                                "sense_id": "86ba2547-8854-304a-9861-4495be012f8e",
                                "text": "This is enough & too much, that when the Romaniſts doe boaſt that their iuriſdiction is ſpirituall, it is eaſy to ſhewe that there is nothing more contrary to the order inſtitute of Chriſte, and that it hath no more likeneſſe to the auncient cuſtome than darkneſſe hath to light."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "da6a8d87-bbef-43c5-91aa-9d79a756a735",
                                "sense_id": "86ba2547-8854-304a-9861-4495be012f8e",
                                "text": "In quarrels with the Pope if the Clergy ſhould diſown to be ſubject to that temporal Prince who conteſts with him, if they refuſe to contribute for the defence of the Nation, if they foment any ſecret deſigns at the Popes command, then the ſtricteſt Romaniſt would preſently ſee the inſecurity of that Kingdom."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9765627d-9618-4d17-bb04-7f759e69e31e",
                                "sense_id": "86ba2547-8854-304a-9861-4495be012f8e",
                                "text": "The manner of the Romanists however hanging their Churches with red Damask, & making Musick in a regular Orchestra there—is a despicable Effort—and defeats its own purpose completely, by turning the house of God into a Theatre […]."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "6fe98c6d-f74a-34cb-90b1-8e2727a35171",
                        "entry_id": "a623aed1-db71-3760-8b8d-86cf47dbeedd",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A scholar of Roman law and jurisprudence."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "0d7db501-fb32-42db-bb60-ca2f689417d8",
                                "sense_id": "6fe98c6d-f74a-34cb-90b1-8e2727a35171",
                                "text": "The foundations of present views of Roman civil procedure were laid by the Austrian Romanist Moriz Wlassak [...]"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "2eb6abbb-7f36-3466-af64-74fc29029244",
                        "entry_id": "a623aed1-db71-3760-8b8d-86cf47dbeedd",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A scholar of Roman history and culture."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "399032c2-8fb7-3336-8ce4-ac9ed594d79a",
                        "entry_id": "a623aed1-db71-3760-8b8d-86cf47dbeedd",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A scholar of Romance languages; a Romanicist."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "75209a48-7004-4175-9de1-bc2b1b9c509b",
                                "sense_id": "399032c2-8fb7-3336-8ce4-ac9ed594d79a",
                                "text": "The principal magazines devoted to the subject are—Jahrbuch für romanische und englische Literatur (ed. Wolff, Ebert, and Lembcke), later only für romanische Literatur; Archiv für das Studium der neueren Sprachen (ed. Herrig), of a more popular character; Romania (a quarterly, ed. Gaston Paris and Paul Meyer, since 1872), contains ariticles of the most eminent Romanists; Revue des Langues Romanes (Montpellier, from 1870 onwards), chiefly devoted to Provençal; Romanische Studien (ed. Boehmer); Zeitschrift für romanische Philologie (ed. Gröber, since 1877); and Romanische Forschungen (ed. Vollmöller, since 1884)."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
